 * This project handles startup code & linker script manually.
 * arm-none-eabi-gcc is called for cross-compilation.
 * openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f target/stm32f7x.cfg -c "program main.bin 0x08000000 verify reset exit"
 * Left: arm-none-eabi-gdb main.elf
(gdb) target remote localhost:3333
 *
 * visit "gcc.gnu.org" for commands and controlled compilation
 * arm-none-eabi-gcc -c -mcpu=cortex-m4 -mthumb main.c -o main.o : to stop at compilation, no linking
 * arm-none-eabi-gcc -S -mcpu=cortex-m4 -mthumb main.c -o main.s : to stop at assembly
 *
 * Makefile can be used to automate build commands, only commands written in make file will be executed
 *
 * To view main.o the ELF file, arm-none-eabi-objdump then select the portion to view
 * arm-none-eabi-objdump -d main.o > main_log : read main_log file, assembly codes for every operation performed
 *
 *
 * ################################################################################################################
 * */
